{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570242412,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abca3ffePbIpjwQOl85imo","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b89239001zGLylX5nnAQ939","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abca3ffePbIpjwQOl85imo","messageID":"msg_1d4b886e4001EtaW1F8ZV1V62L","type":"tool","id":"call_32e1b10708024cf99c2c67c2","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - residual-limits-4 (residual limits after 014 and 015)\ndescription: Tracks the residual-limits-4 lineage of the segment-four command-surfacing research on the built state after phases 014 and 015.\ntrigger_phrases: []\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n# Deep Research Strategy - residual-limits-4\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nLane label `residual-limits-4`: what still limits command surfacing after phases 014 (review remediation) and 015 (health default and brief refinements) are built. Three angles: what the reader sees on each of six CLIs, what the hook and brief cost, and what still makes the advisor less useful than it could be across CLIs. Each recommendation must name files, a measured gain and a proof check; anything unmeasured is labelled a hypothesis.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nResidual limits on the built state after phases 014 and 015. Read-first sources are `P/goal.md`, `P/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md` sections 3 and 4, `P/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md`, `P/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/implementation-summary.md` and their scratch after files, then the code at HEAD those summaries name. Anything ranked, built, declined or waiting in segments one, two and three is closed unless a new measurement changes its disposition, in which case the rank and the measurement are named. No tracked file is edited and no live arm is started.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] KQ1: What does the reader see on each of claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh at HEAD after phases 014 and 015, and which runtime still loses the command, the policy or the skill, or reports the brief as unknown?\n- [ ] KQ2: What is the live brief size per prompt and the hook latency at HEAD after phase 015, and which bytes or milliseconds can be removed without losing the command, the policy or the skill?\n- [ ] KQ3: Which residual limits still make the advisor less useful across the CLIs, and which change is worth building next, with the files, the measured gain and the check that proves it?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending or re-measuring anything ranked, built, declined or waiting in `research.md`, `research-segment-2.md` or `research-segment-3.md`, unless a new measurement changes its disposition and the rank is named.\n- Re-measuring the two segment-four lanes: richer command embedding text (rank 10) and in-process timing of the degraded scorer (rank 6). Those own separate lineages.\n- Changing scorer weights, corpus labels, pins, the Python scorer, or any tracked file.\n- Starting a model CLI session, an arena, a live arm, or pulling/starting Ollama.\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout numbers only, through committed scripts.\n- Editing files outside this lineage directory.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below with every key question answered or explicitly carried forward.\n- Eight iterations at most; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nKQ1: the reader's experience per runtime on the built state after 014 and 015, starting from the final behaviour arm summaries and the delivery evidence each runtime writes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- Phase 015 built segment-three ranks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9 and 11. Suite 183 files, 1755 passed. Floors unchanged: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, eval `[160,50,21,5]`, holdout rows published 44 to 0.\n- Final arm rescored with the phase 015 scorer: `claude` unsafe 0 of 0 no-changed-path, `devin` 2 and 1, `dsh` 2 and 2, `opencode` 2 and 0, `pi` 1 and 1. Codex not measurable because hooks are unapproved.\n- Open limitations carried into this lane: live brief bytes not measured (T030 exited 2 with `degraded_brief`); OpenCode `deliveryUnknown` is 24; DSH has 1 unscored run; Codex 0 of 24 delivery.\n- Read-only boundary: this lineage writes only inside `.../lineages/residual-limits-4/`.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: `P/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/summary-final.json`, `P/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/scratch/summary-final-after.json`, `P/015.../scratch/before.txt`, `P/015.../scratch/live-heads.txt`, `P/015.../scratch/render-entries-after.json`, `ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\n- Reuse candidates: committed capture and scoring scripts; the health record read through `advisor_status`; the committed render probes in phase 015 scratch.\n- Integration points: `ADV/lib/render.ts`, `ADV/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`.\n- Constraints and risks: no tracked writes; holdout text never read; no live arm or model session.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 16 tool calls, 20 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Question injection surface: local `inbox.jsonl`\n- Canonical pause sentinel: local `.deep-research-pause`\n- Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-13T12:45:00Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/residual-limits-4/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/residual-limits-4/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/residual-limits-4/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - residual-limits-4 (residual limits after 014 and 015)\\ndescription: Tracks the residual-limits-4 lineage of the segment-four command-surfacing research on the built state after phases 014 and 015.\\ntrigger_phrases: []\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n# Deep Research Strategy - residual-limits-4\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\nLane label `residual-limits-4`: what still limits command surfacing after phases 014 (review remediation) and 015 (health default and brief refinements) are built. Three angles: what the reader sees on each of six CLIs, what the hook and brief cost, and what still makes the advisor less useful than it could be across CLIs. Each recommendation must name files, a measured gain and a proof check; anything unmeasured is labelled a hypothesis.\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nResidual limits on the built state after phases 014 and 015. Read-first sources are `P/goal.md`, `P/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md` sections 3 and 4, `P/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md`, `P/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/implementation-summary.md` and their scratch after files, then the code at HEAD those summaries name. Anything ranked, built, declined or waiting in segments one, two and three is closed unless a new measurement changes its disposition, in which case the rank and the measurement are named. No tracked file is edited and no live arm is started.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] KQ1: What does the reader see on each of claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh at HEAD after phases 014 and 015, and which runtime still loses the command, the policy or the skill, or reports the brief as unknown?\\n- [ ] KQ2: What is the live brief size per prompt and the hook latency at HEAD after phase 015, and which bytes or milliseconds can be removed without losing the command, the policy or the skill?\\n- [ ] KQ3: Which residual limits still make the advisor less useful across the CLIs, and which change is worth building next, with the files, the measured gain and the check that proves it?\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-recommending or re-measuring anything ranked, built, declined or waiting in `research.md`, `research-segment-2.md` or `research-segment-3.md`, unless a new measurement changes its disposition and the rank is named.\\n- Re-measuring the two segment-four lanes: richer command embedding text (rank 10) and in-process timing of the degraded scorer (rank 6). Those own separate lineages.\\n- Changing scorer weights, corpus labels, pins, the Python scorer, or any tracked file.\\n- Starting a model CLI session, an arena, a live arm, or pulling/starting Ollama.\\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout numbers only, through committed scripts.\\n- Editing files outside this lineage directory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below with every key question answered or explicitly carried forward.\\n- Eight iterations at most; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nKQ1: the reader's experience per runtime on the built state after 014 and 015, starting from the final behaviour arm summaries and the delivery evidence each runtime writes.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n- Phase 015 built segment-three ranks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9 and 11. Suite 183 files, 1755 passed. Floors unchanged: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, eval `[160,50,21,5]`, holdout rows published 44 to 0.\\n- Final arm rescored with the phase 015 scorer: `claude` unsafe 0 of 0 no-changed-path, `devin` 2 and 1, `dsh` 2 and 2, `opencode` 2 and 0, `pi` 1 and 1. Codex not measurable because hooks are unapproved.\\n- Open limitations carried into this lane: live brief bytes not measured (T030 exited 2 with `degraded_brief`); OpenCode `deliveryUnknown` is 24; DSH has 1 unscored run; Codex 0 of 24 delivery.\\n- Read-only boundary: this lineage writes only inside `.../lineages/residual-limits-4/`.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: `P/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/summary-final.json`, `P/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/scratch/summary-final-after.json`, `P/015.../scratch/before.txt`, `P/015.../scratch/live-heads.txt`, `P/015.../scratch/render-entries-after.json`, `ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\\n- Reuse candidates: committed capture and scoring scripts; the health record read through `advisor_status`; the committed render probes in phase 015 scratch.\\n- Integration points: `ADV/lib/render.ts`, `ADV/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`.\\n- Constraints and risks: no tracked writes; holdout text never read; no live arm or model session.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 16 tool calls, 20 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\\n- Question injection surface: local `inbox.jsonl`\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: local `.deep-research-pause`\\n- Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-13T12:45:00Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/residual-limits-4/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570228281,"end":1794570242412}}}}
